# darkstr 0029 — soft residual: enable live WebGL context (LibreWolf hardening undo)
#
# Proof matrices on Mini LibreWolf (headed + marionette) report getContext('webgl'|
# 'webgl2') => null with creationError "WebGL is currently disabled." even under
# Homogeneous/hooks-off and after webgl.disabled=false + blocklist unlock (tip
# 0f8b3b3 soft FAIL). Canvas 2D depth already PASSes — GPU/display fine.
#
# Root cause (verified tip 0f8b3b3): that Err string is NOT from
# StaticPrefs::webgl_disabled() when prefs show false. LibreWolf-patched
# ClientWebGLContext.cpp:
#   if (mCanvasElement && !StaticPrefs::webgl_disabled()) {
#     if (!IsWebGLAllowed(...)) {
#       return Err("WebGL is currently disabled.");
#     }
#   }
# IsWebGLAllowed uses StaticPrefs::librewolf_webgl_prompt() (pref name
# librewolf.webgl.prompt; C++ getter dots/hyphens → underscores). When true,
# WebGL is blocked until a per-origin permission doorhanger is Allowed —
# marionette/automation never clicks Allow → null context. Pref-layer 0029 was
# incomplete without unlocking the LW permission prompt gate.
#
# Corrected facts (tip-up after soft XOR FAIL on tip 0f8b3b3; keep prior facts):
#   - nsIGfxInfo status 2 = FEATURE_STATUS_UNKNOWN (not blocked). Blocked starts at
#     FEATURE_BLOCKED_DRIVER_VERSION=3, FEATURE_BLOCKED_DEVICE=4, …
#   - gfx.blocklist.all > 0 forces block-all features; < 0 ignores feature
#     blocklisting. Pref is mirror:once / AtStartup — must be in cfg before gfx
#     init; runtime set after startup is completeness-only (startup cfg is SoT).
#   - LibreWolf lw/librewolf.cfg may already have pref("webgl.disabled", false);
#     that alone is insufficient when blocklist/forbid prefs OR
#     librewolf.webgl.prompt still kill context.
#   - StaticPrefList.yaml: librewolf.webgl.prompt / librewolf.webgl.prompt.hide
#     (RelaxedAtomicBool, mirror:always; prompt default true → doorhanger gate).
#
# Fix (chrome-only, product-level — both Homogeneous and Pollution):
#   DarkstrModeXor.applyModeEffects → _ensureWebGlContextPrefs():
#     webgl.disabled=false
#     webgl.force-enabled=true
#     webgl.forbid-hardware=false / webgl.forbid-software=false (if prefs exist)
#     try Services.prefs.setIntPref("gfx.blocklist.all", -1) (runtime; cfg SoT)
#     librewolf.webgl.prompt=false (unlock + set; if pref exists)
#     librewolf.webgl.prompt.hide=true (secondary; if pref exists)
#   Diagnostics: darkstr.webgl.ensureApplied / darkstr.webgl.lastStatus
#     (enriched ~180–400 chars: WEBGL_OPENGL + WEBGL2 numeric status + failureId;
#      map 1=OK 2=UNKNOWN 3=BLOCKED_DRIVER … via nsIGfxInfo;
#      includes librewolf.webgl.prompt=<value>)
#   darkstr.cfg + lw append: matching defaultPref including gfx.blocklist.all=-1
#     + librewolf.webgl.prompt=false (+ prompt.hide)
#
# Claims: live WebGL context available for Proof XOR (UNMASKED + apple caps via
# existing 0017/0023 when Pollution+hooks SubsequentNav). Firefox persona only.
# Non-claims: extension lists / shader precision / fail-closed unknown getParameter
# (WebExt richer); no Chrome cosplay; no software-GL invention if GPU process dead.
#
# Chrome JS only; no XUL relink. Brand: darkstr — not official LibreWolf.
# Train: Firefox FIREFOX_156_0_1_RELEASE / LibreWolf 156.0.1-1 (ported from 155)

